PRETABLE_5 -- pvrrenderexit, test-variant table 5 (repair 5: the swap body's statement-deletion closure, the right end from
above, a negative span start; 148 rows).
Written BEFORE table 5 runs: its mtime must precede every RESULT file in table5/ (the frozen probe is copied there first and is
older).  INSTRUMENT: table5/probe148_frozen.py, cmp-identical to regress/pvr_zwrite_probe.py when this was written.
INSTRUMENT_MD5 84fe7386d80139de97ec7026bbe23e7f table5/probe148_frozen.py
Baseline: dev_pvr.c.fix5 (== GXEMUL-SEC src/devices/dev_pvr.c).  Variants: pvr_table5.py -- table 4's 146 and repair 5's 44 (the
17 deletion cells not built before, N1s, the 26 compound survivors).
EVERY prediction is EXACT -- the full red set, none = all 148 green -- except Y2s/Y2t/Y4s/Y4t (undefined behaviour, NOT
PREDICTED, counted in no tally).  The 140 rows that carry over: the red set MEASURED by table 4 (../r4_20261105/table4/SCORES.txt)
and, for the 44, by step 1 on the shipped 140-row probe (meas140/SCORES.txt).  The repair-5 rows -- 8 of them, the two
optional left-end rows included (kept on a measured delta, meas_cand/SCORES.txt) -- DERIVED per variant (pvr_table5.py NEW5),
each Z-on row and Z-off twin listed BY NAME: ramp8hi_r_end, zramp8hi_r_end, ramp8hi_l_end, zramp8hi_l_end, negx_n_start, znegx_n_start, texnegx_n_start, ztnegx_n_start.
Of the eleven depth compounds the ruling predicted red, SEVEN are predicted red here (simpleline's) and texturedline's FOUR green.
190 variants: 186 predicted, 156 predicted red, 30 predicted green, 4 NOT PREDICTED.
Legs: base 148/148; HEAD (det_20261104/dev_pvr.c.HEAD) 70/148 SYMPTOM=PRESENT -- MEASURED already, its red set is the one below;
null media CONTROL=FAIL: /bin/true 9/148, an absent binary 0/148, /bin/false 1/148.
EXCLUDED and named (not built; undefined behaviour, DERIVED -- codex pass 5 counted 13 such forms and did not list them):
   simpleline `r1 = r2` -> `r1 /= r2`           RAMP row 60: r2 = 0 (green) -> 255/0, column 440 drawn
   simpleline `tmpf = g1` -> `tmpf /= g1`       a constant-red span: tmpf = r1 = 255, g1 = 0 -> g2 = inf, the second pixel on
   simpleline `g1 = g2` -> `g1 /= g2`           a constant-red span: 0/0
   simpleline `g2 = tmpf` -> `g2 /= tmpf`       a constant-red span: 0/0
   simpleline `tmpf = b1` -> `tmpf /= b1`       a constant-red span: tmpf = g1 = 0, b1 = 0 -> 0/0
   simpleline `b1 = b2` -> `b1 /= b2`           a constant-red span: 0/0
   simpleline `b2 = tmpf` -> `b2 /= tmpf`       a constant-red span: 0/0
   texturedline `tmpf = u1` -> `tmpf /= u1`     SWAP textured (u = v = 0): tmpf = z1 = 2.0, u1 = 0 -> u2 = inf
   texturedline `u1 = u2` -> `u1 /= u2`         SWAP textured: 0/0
   texturedline `u2 = tmpf` -> `u2 /= tmpf`     SWAP textured: 0/0
   texturedline `tmpf = v1` -> `tmpf /= v1`     SWAP textured: tmpf = u1 = 0, v1 = 0 -> 0/0
   texturedline `v1 = v2` -> `v1 /= v2`         SWAP textured: 0/0
   texturedline `v2 = tmpf` -> `v2 /= tmpf`     SWAP textured: 0/0

CHANNELS of the 8 repair-5 rows (pixel, want; the variants that move it and the observable -- DERIVED, every end exact in binary):
  ramp8hi r end (448,60) BLUE -- RAMP8 (z 3, 2, 3; magenta, green, magenta) row 60 arrives 448.0 / 440.0, swapped: column 448 carries
    vertex 1's z 3.0, and COVERHI (Z-on, z 4.0, blue) drawn after it passes there.  Red when the depth stored at 448 exceeds 4.0, so
    magenta stays: DTs_z (`tmpf = z1;` deleted: z2 = the original x1, 448.0), CZs_tadd 451, CZs_tmul 1344, CZs_tdiv 149.33, CZs_z2add
    5, CZs_z2mul 6.
  zramp8hi r end (448,60) BLUE -- COVERHI (Z-on) FIRST stores 4.0; RAMP8 Z-off fails there with 3.0.  Red when RAMP8 passes: the same
    six z values; Ps (`<= z + 1`: 4.0 <= 4.0); a depth test skipped for the Z-off span (M13, M26); COVERHI storing no depth (M3, M15,
    M6, M7); B1_exit (the session ends).
  ramp8hi l end (440,60) BLUE -- column 440 carries vertex 2's z 2.0; COVERHI passes.  Red: CZs_z1add (z1 = 5) and CZs_z1mul (6) --
    green stays; X1s (`int x = x1 + 1`: COVERHI and RAMP8 both start at 441, so nothing draws 440: black).
  zramp8hi l end (440,60) BLUE -- RAMP8 Z-off fails at 440 with 2.0 against 4.0.  Red: CZs_z1add, CZs_z1mul (5 and 6 pass: green),
    X1s (440 undrawn), M13, M26, M3, M15, M6, M7, B1_exit; not Ps (4.0 <= 2.0 + 1 fails).
  negx n start (1,60) RED -- NEGX (green, red, green; z 2.0) row 60 arrives -1.0 / 1.0, forward: columns -1 and 0 are clipped but still
    advance the colour, so column 1 is the third step, vertex 2's red.  Red: N1s, B2s, X1s (a start of -1 + c truncates to 0: the
    midpoint, 0x7be0, at column 1), E1s (`x < x2`: column 1 not drawn), M19 (`x > 1`), O1s (`x1 < 0 || x2 < 0` returns), W4s (`x1 < 0
    && x2 < 2` returns).  As (`x1 - 1`) puts (382.5, -127.5, 0) at column 1, which CLAMPS to red: green.
  znegx n start -- the Z-off twin: the same, plus B1_exit, M11 and M12 (the Z-off span not drawn), W1s (Z-off `x > 1`), V6s (Z-off
    `x <= x2 - 2`); V5s (Z-off `x1 - 2`) clamps to red: green.
  texnegx n start (1,60) GREEN -- NEGX textured, u 0 -> 0.5 (du12 0.25): column 1 samples u 0.5, texel (4,0).  Red: B2t and X1t (u 0.25:
    texel (2,0), linear 0x500000), At (u 0.75: texel (6,0), linear 0x500004) -- both never stored -- E1t, M23, O1t, W4t.
  ztnegx n start -- the Z-off twin: the same, plus B1_exit, M11, M28 (not drawn), W1t, V7t (Z-off column 1 not drawn), V2t (Z-off `x1 <
    0 && x2 < 2` returns), V5t (Z-off start at 1 with u 0: texel (0,0), red).
  Every other variant leaves these eight green -- the swap-body deletions but DTs_z, the RGB and UV compounds (colour only: COVERHI
  covers Z-on, RAMP8 fails Z-off), and texturedline's four depth compounds CZt_* (ramp8hi is untextured; measured green on the
  candidate rows, meas_cand/SCORES.txt).

